From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rtl8733bs: build without warnings

- 889 -Wmissing-prototypes: the vendor shares global functions between
  files without header declarations. The Makefile turns that warning
  and -Wmissing-declarations off. (This driver's Makefile passes
  EXTRA_CFLAGS to ccflags-y, so the flag takes effect.)
- 61 -Wempty-body: PHYDM_DBG, PHYDM_DBG_F, PHYDM_PRINT_ADDR, RF_DBG and
  DBG_COUNTER expand to nothing in this build, which leaves
  "if (x) MACRO(...);" with an empty body. They now expand to
  do {} while (0).
- 9 -Waddress:
  - lock is the first member of struct sta_info, so "&psta->lock !=
    NULL" tested psta. With -fno-delete-null-pointer-checks it stayed in
    the code; it now reads "psta";
  - the debug command parsers tested rows of char input[][16], which
    are never NULL. Remove those checks and keep the existing scans
    unconditional, including when strsep produces empty fields.
- 3 -Wmisleading-indentation (rtw_recv.c, rtw_efuse.c, phydm_dfs.c): the
  statements already ran once after the loop or the if; only the
  indentation is corrected.
- -Wenum-conversion: rxagg_mode gets RX_AGG_DMA instead of
  HALMAC_RX_AGG_MODE_DMA; both are 1.
- 3 -Wempty-body on explicit empty statements: braces instead.
- -Wunused-function: nl80211_chan_width_str() is only used by debug
  output that this build compiles out; it is marked __maybe_unused.

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 74bf739..cee469c 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@ EXTRA_CFLAGS += $(USER_EXTRA_CFLAGS)
 #EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wshadow -Wpointer-arith -Wcast-qual -Wstrict-prototypes -Wmissing-prototypes
 
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-unused-variable
+# Vendor functions are shared between files without header declarations.
+EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-missing-prototypes -Wno-missing-declarations
 #EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-unused-value
 #EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-unused-label
 #EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-unused-parameter
